A||||9||loafer87gt||Anyone had a Maaco paintjob?||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||02-12-2001||11:25 PM||||Just wondering. I know you get what you pay for, but they have a special on this week to get your whole car painted for $260 canadian!! I read somewhere that a guy had a paintjob done that peeled really badly. What causes this, is this just poor paint or what? (I know nothing about autobody stuff)||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||02-12-2001||11:31 PM||||Ive mentioned this before. I own my own body shop and some car dealers jobs for cheap cars go to Maaco after I sand and mask them. They spray it for almost less than I can buy good paint. But the dealers just want it to look good long enough to sell, so for long term there not very durable. If you do, sand it and mask as much as you can yourself. They pretty much just wipe off the car and shoot it and there only given like 30 mins to mask each complete car.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||02-12-2001||11:56 PM||||try searching under "maaco" I know that several have had it done, and most are not happy, a few are. If you decide to do it I would upgrade one level up if its not to much more.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ed||02-13-2001||12:05 AM||||One of our club members (former club officer) had his car done at Maaco and it turned out real well.  Metallic green.  Its for sale so you can buy it and see for yourself! (He'll still have two beautiful Fieros and a parts Fiero after it goes, though)<P>Better check for details about what you'll get for that low price.  I doubt it will be the deluxe job for $260.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||02-13-2001||08:12 AM||||I believe Maaco dealers are franchises and quality of work is very dependent on the management.  Ed Parks uses the Maaco shop in Huntsville with good results.<P>I've had good paint jobs at an Earl Sheib shop in Houston and Peach in Birmingham.  I had a terrible one from Fact-o Bake in New Orleans.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||firstfiero||02-13-2001||09:03 AM||||     Macco is probobly what I'm goint to do. From asking around it seems the macco in our area does a good job. From what I understand it's hit or miss. Most of the guys working their our new to the business....some our good and some our bad. I don't have 1000.00+ to put into a paint job right now so macco's going to have to do. :rooeyes:<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000006||Fleabitdog||02-13-2001||03:58 PM||||I was going to get Maaco to paint my red 88GT Blue.  They gave me a price of 625.00 and I paid it that day, I was going to drop my car off next morning. I read the contract when I got home and it said they weren't going to paint any jams. I called them right away and went in and got my money back. Could you imagine a blue car with red jams? Glad I read the contract. I have heard some good stories about Maaco but that really turned me off.||||reg||1
Z||000007||ToddAsh||02-13-2001||08:09 PM||||I've had  couple of cars painted at our local Maaco and was very pleased.I did sanding and primer and went with the same color. Good job for the money. Two of these were beater '78 and '80 Corvettes. Sold them at a profit after using them as winter cars.Great fun. Todd||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ronnie||02-13-2001||10:10 PM||||I had a Suzuki Samarai painted by Maaco coupla years ago has held up pretty good. My father-in -law had his truck painted, looked real good.But my son had his Honda painted this past summer, got a crappy job. Had bad orange peel. They had to re-do his paintjob. But couldn't get all the orange peel out. So, depends on the day you take it I think.<BR>BTW, they wanted $900.00 to paint my GT.<P>------------------<BR>Black '86GT 4spd / Silver '87GT 5spd<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BOTHGTS_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000009||Carrolles||02-14-2001||12:23 AM||||Peach in Birmingham is like Macco.  They have three levels of paint jobs, a basic enamal paint, integrated clearcoat, and base coat/clear coat.<P>They quoted me $670 for a true base coat/ clear coat paint job on my Metalic grey 85SE.  That includes removing the luggage rack etc and painting allthe black areas such as around the rear glass, the mirrors, and lggage rack.  Doesn't soundtoo bad.<P>I had three cars painted with the integrated base/clear system and they looked pretty good and held up well.||||reg||1
